AETHER — Phase 17: Real Data Ingestion Layer (News, Sentiment, Macro Blackout)

Bounded, single-phase prompt, same discipline as Phases 10–16 (Prompts 12–18) in docs/Prompts/. No prior conversation history is available to you — this document is self-contained. Audit first, as always, and do not expand scope beyond what is listed here.

0. Context you must internalize first, and why this phase exists

AETHER is a no-code visual builder for algorithmic trading agents. The frontend (apps/web, Next.js 16 / React 19 / TypeScript / Zustand / @xyflow/react) was frozen across Phases 0–9. Backend work since then (Phases 10–16) made auth, bot persistence, backtesting, the scheduled live paper-trading loop, billing/credits, presets/marketplace, and LLM reasoning for four Layer III intelligence agents (technical-agent, sentiment-agent, macro-agent, event-agent) all genuinely real.

The gap this phase closes, stated plainly because Phase 16's own report already flagged it and you must not repeat the mistake of pretending otherwise:

apps/engine/app/nodes/universal.py's "data" layer branch is what currently backs news-stream, social-sentiment, and macro-calendar — the three Layer I "Data Collection" nodes that are supposed to sit upstream of the sentiment/macro/event agents in a real graph. Today, that branch does not fetch anything from the outside world. It fabricates a NewsFeed-shaped output on every single call:

python
"sentimentScore": 0.65 if rsi < 40 else (-0.65 if rsi > 60 else 0.0),
"blackoutActive": False,

This means: sentimentScore is a repackaged technical indicator, not sentiment. blackoutActive is permanently False — no code path anywhere in the system has ever set it to True outside of a hand-constructed unit test. The four LLM agents you built in Phases 14–16 are real, hardened, credit-metered, audited — and they are reasoning over a number that is secretly RSI wearing a trenchcoat.

Your job this phase: make news-stream, social-sentiment, and macro-calendar real Layer I data-collection nodes, each with its own dedicated class (not the generic UniversalNode stub), backed by:

Real crypto news headlines, fetched on a schedule, cached in Postgres, scored for sentiment with a real (non-LLM, free, deterministic) NLP sentiment model — VADER.
A real, curated macro event calendar (FOMC meetings, US CPI releases, US NFP releases) — seeded data, not a live third-party API dependency, for reasons explained in §3 — that genuinely drives blackoutActive for the first time in this project's history.
Wiring both into the compiled graph exactly the way ohlcv-feed already is, so sentiment-agent / macro-agent / event-agent need zero code changes — they already consume NewsFeed-typed upstream output via find_upstream(ctx, "NewsFeed"), and this phase's job is only to make the thing they find be real.

What this phase deliberately does NOT do: it does not touch LLM reasoning, credits, BYOK, the gateway, flow-agent, contrarian-agent, ML/RL, OCULUS, or ChromaDB. It does not add a second sentiment provider or a paid news API. It does not try to build a comprehensive global macro calendar — it seeds three specific, high-impact, well-known recurring US event types, because a shaky live calendar-scraping integration is worse than an honestly-scoped static one for a phase whose entire point is truthfulness about what's real.

