4. Task 2 — News ingestion: fetch, sentiment-score, cache
4.1 Data source

Use CryptoCompare's public News API (https://min-api.cryptocompare.com/data/v2/news/?lang=EN) — it requires no API key for reasonable request volumes, returns real crypto news headlines with a body, title, url, published_on (unix timestamp), categories (comma-separated, from which you can derive a rough symbols tag by checking for BTC/ETH substrings), and a stable id per article for dedup. Confirm this endpoint's exact current response shape yourself by fetching it once during development — do not assume the shape from memory; API response shapes drift.

4.2 Sentiment scoring: VADER

Add vaderSentiment to apps/engine/requirements.txt. VADER (vaderSentiment.vaderSentiment.SentimentIntensityAnalyzer) is a free, deterministic, lexicon-and-rule-based sentiment analyzer — not an LLM, not an API call, no cost, no rate limit, runs in milliseconds. This is the correct tool here: real NLP, zero incremental cost or latency risk to the ingestion job, and it composes cleanly with the separate, already-real LLM reasoning layer built in Phases 14–16 — VADER produces the sentimentScore that feeds the deterministic baseline and the LLM's context, exactly as the previously-fake RSI-derived number did structurally, except now the number means what it says.

Run analyzer.polarity_scores(title + ". " + body_snippet) per article, storing compound, pos, neg, neu on the news_items row.

